            <ArticleTitle>Tuberous Sclerosis in Identical Twins.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>127-128</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tuberous sclerosis was, observed in six year old identical twin brothers born with single placenta and a single amnion. Both had adenoma sebaceum shagreen patches, ash leaf spots and progressive mental deterioration. One of them had a verrucous pigmented nevus on the, left temple and recurrent localized motor seizures.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
